  "summary": "A developmental hydrofluoroolefin (HFO) fluid for two-phase immersion cooling. It boils at 48.9 °C, has a GWP of 10 (AR6), and has no flash point and no flammability limits. Chemours positions it as a replacement for PFPEs, HFEs, fluoroketones and PFCs in immersion cooling. It is a developmental product: confirm commercial availability with Chemours.",
